{
  "paragraphs": [
    "calibration_ok: 118 of 118 rows have known values (100.0% coverage).",
    "At k = 20, mean shared-label agreement is 67.1% when weighting positive anchor\u2013label pairs, and 47.6% when weighting labels equally. Mean individual label lift is 0.9511 and equal-label lift is 0.838. Mean lift is not aggregate purity divided by aggregate chance.",
    "true: 93 known positives; 93 evaluable positive anchors have 81.5% mean agreement, versus 78.8% reference prevalence (lift 1.034). An average of 20 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "false: 25 known positives; 25 evaluable positive anchors have 13.6% mean agreement, versus 21.2% reference prevalence (lift 0.6419). An average of 20 of 20 neighbors have known annotations. Large lift for a rare label can coexist with low agreement.",
    "Known-neighbor coverage at this k is 100.0%. Unknown neighbors are excluded from agreement denominators; missing annotations can bias the result.",
    "The saved null comparison gives an empirical one-sided p-value of 1 for macro_lift. This tests the specified shuffle, not semantic understanding; use the combined multiple-testing table and practical effect sizes when judging the finding.",
    "The probe panel measures recoverability on a held-out split. Compare each model with its baseline; recoverability and nearest-neighbor usefulness answer different questions.",
    "baseline: balanced_accuracy 0.5, macro_f1 0.4231; 30 held-out test rows (or the macro summary of supported binary tags).",
    "linear: balanced_accuracy 0.5227, macro_f1 0.4976; 30 held-out test rows (or the macro summary of supported binary tags).",
    "For paired_micro_purity at k = 20, A is 0.6712 and B is 0.6725, with B\u2212A 0.001271 across 118 paired anchors. Conditional 95% interval: -0.003651 to 0.00668; higher is better for this measure. This does not rank overall embedding quality.",
    "Embedding A normalization comparison on identical held-out rows: raw_standardized: balanced_accuracy 0.5227, unit: balanced_accuracy 0.4148, unit_standardized: balanced_accuracy 0.4375, norm_only: balanced_accuracy 0.4716. Direction-only and magnitude-only scores describe accessible information for these pipelines; fit telemetry does not establish encoder-training stability.",
    "Embedding B normalization comparison on identical held-out rows: raw_standardized: balanced_accuracy 0.7386, unit: balanced_accuracy 0.5284, unit_standardized: balanced_accuracy 0.7216, norm_only: balanced_accuracy 0.4943. Direction-only and magnitude-only scores describe accessible information for these pipelines; fit telemetry does not establish encoder-training stability.",
    "In the raw_euclidean filtration for embedding A, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 1 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "In the raw_euclidean filtration for embedding B, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 0 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "In the unit_chordal filtration for embedding A, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 2 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "In the unit_chordal filtration for embedding B, the shuffled-minus-observed component variation gap exceeds 0.02 at 1 of 6 evaluated radii, across 2 sampled cohorts. This is descriptive annotation organization across correlated scales, not a topology significance test or a semantic quality grade.",
    "Next: compare feature measurements across scales, check probe gains against baselines, or summarize a selected region. Shared labels and correlated features can suggest patterns, but do not establish why the model retrieved an item."
